{"surah": 90, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "لَآ أُقْسِمُ بِهَٰذَا ٱلْبَلَدِ ", "translation": "I swear by this city [i.e., Makkah] –", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَآ", "translit": "ٓāَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أُقْسِمُ", "translit": "ُmِsْqُaʾ", "root": "قسم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَلَدِ", "translit": "ِdَlَbْlٱ", "root": "بلد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَأَنتَ حِلٌّۢ بِهَٰذَا ٱلْبَلَدِ ", "translation": "And you, [O Muḥammad], are free of restriction in this city –", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَنتَ", "translit": "َtnَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "حِلٌّۢ", "translit": "ٌّۢlِḥ", "root": "حلل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِهَٰذَا", "translit": "āَhdَٰhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْبَلَدِ", "translit": "ِdَlَbْlٱ", "root": "بلد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَوَالِدٍ وَمَا وَلَدَ ", "translation": "And [by] the father[1] and that which was born [of him],", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَوَالِدٍ", "translit": "ٍdِlāَwَw", "root": "ولد"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَلَدَ", "translit": "َdَlَw", "root": "ولد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "لَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ فِى كَبَدٍ ", "translation": "We have certainly created man into hardship.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَقَدْ", "translit": "ْdَqَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "خَلَقْنَا", "translit": "āَnْqَlَhk", "root": "خلق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنَ", "translit": "َnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "كَبَدٍ", "translit": "ٍdَbَk", "root": "كبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "أَيَحْسَبُ أَن لَّن يَقْدِرَ عَلَيْهِ أَحَدٌ ", "translation": "Does he think that never will anyone overcome him?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَيَحْسَبُ", "translit": "ُbَsْḥَyَaʾ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّن", "translit": "nَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَقْدِرَ", "translit": "َrِdْqَy", "root": "قدر"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِ", "translit": "ِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "أَحَدٌ", "translit": "ٌdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "يَقُولُ أَهْلَكْتُ مَالًا لُّبَدًا ", "translation": "He says, \"I have spent wealth in abundance.\"", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَقُولُ", "translit": "ُlwُqَy", "root": "قول"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَهْلَكْتُ", "translit": "ُtْkَlْhَaʾ", "root": "هلك"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَالًا", "translit": "āًlāَm", "root": "مول"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لُّبَدًا", "translit": "āًdَbُّl", "root": "لبد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "أَيَحْسَبُ أَن لَّمْ يَرَهُۥٓ أَحَدٌ ", "translation": "Does he think that no one has seen him?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَيَحْسَبُ", "translit": "ُbَsْḥَyَaʾ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّمْ", "translit": "ْmَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَرَهُۥٓ", "translit": "ٓۥُhَrَy", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَحَدٌ", "translit": "ٌdَḥَaʾ", "root": "احد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "أَلَمْ نَجْعَل لَّهُۥ عَيْنَيْنِ ", "translation": "Have We not made for him two eyes?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَلَمْ", "translit": "ْmَlَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَجْعَل", "translit": "lَʿعْjgَn", "root": "جعل"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "عَيْنَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَnْyَʿع", "root": "عين"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "وَلِسَانًا وَشَفَتَيْنِ ", "translation": "And a tongue and two lips?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلِسَانًا", "translit": "āًnāَsِlَw", "root": "لسن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَشَفَتَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَtَfَhsَw", "root": "شفه"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَهَدَيْنَٰهُ ٱلنَّجْدَيْنِ ", "translation": "And have shown him the two ways?[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَهَدَيْنَٰهُ", "translit": "ُhَٰnْyَdَhَw", "root": "هدي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلنَّجْدَيْنِ", "translit": "ِnْyَdْjgَّnlٱ", "root": "نجد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "فَلَا ٱقْتَحَمَ ٱلْعَقَبَةَ ", "translation": "But he has not broken through the difficult pass.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَا", "translit": "āَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱقْتَحَمَ", "translit": "َmَḥَtْqٱ", "root": "قحم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْعَقَبَةَ", "translit": "َẗَbَqَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عقب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "وَمَآ أَدْرَىٰكَ مَا ٱلْعَقَبَةُ ", "translation": "And what can make you know what is [breaking through] the difficult pass?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَمَآ", "translit": "ٓāَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَدْرَىٰكَ", "translit": "َkٰàَrْdَaʾ", "root": "دري"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْعَقَبَةُ", "translit": "ُẗَbَqَʿعْlٱ", "root": "عقب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "فَكُّ رَقَبَةٍ ", "translation": "It is the freeing of a slave", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَكُّ", "translit": "ُّkَf", "root": "فكك"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "رَقَبَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَbَqَr", "root": "رقب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "أَوْ إِطْعَٰمٌ فِى يَوْمٍ ذِى مَسْغَبَةٍ ", "translation": "Or feeding on a day of severe hunger", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِطْعَٰمٌ", "translit": "ٌmَٰʿعْṭِiʾ", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِى", "translit": "àِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَوْمٍ", "translit": "ٍmْwَy", "root": "يوم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ذِى", "translit": "àِhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "مَسْغَبَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَbَغْsَm", "root": "سغب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "يَتِيمًا ذَا مَقْرَبَةٍ ", "translation": "An orphan of near relationship", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَتِيمًا", "translit": "āًmyِtَy", "root": "يتم"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ذَا", "translit": "āَhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مَقْرَبَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَbَrْqَm", "root": "قرب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "أَوْ مِسْكِينًا ذَا مَتْرَبَةٍ ", "translation": "Or a needy person in misery", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَوْ", "translit": "ْwَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مِسْكِينًا", "translit": "āًnyِkْsِm", "root": "سكن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ذَا", "translit": "āَhd", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَتْرَبَةٍ", "translit": "ٍẗَbَrْtَm", "root": "ترب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "ثُمَّ كَانَ مِنَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلصَّبْرِ وَتَوَاصَوْا۟ بِٱلْمَرْحَمَةِ ", "translation": "And then being among those who believed and advised one another to patience and advised one another to compassion.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ثُمَّ", "translit": "َّmُht", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مِنَ", "translit": "َnِm", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "وَتَوَاصَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَṣāَwَtَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "بِٱلصَّبْرِ", "translit": "ِrْbَّṣlٱِb", "root": "صبر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "وَتَوَاصَوْا۟", "translit": "۟āْwَṣāَwَtَw", "root": "وصي"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "بِٱلْمَرْحَمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmَḥْrَmْlٱِb", "root": "رحم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْمَيْمَنَةِ ", "translation": "Those are the companions of the right.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أُو۟لَٰٓئِكَ", "translit": "َkِyʾَٰٓl۟wُaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱلْمَيْمَنَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَnَmْyَmْlٱ", "root": "يمن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "وَٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا هُمْ أَصْحَٰبُ ٱلْمَشْـَٔمَةِ ", "translation": "But they who disbelieved in Our signs - those are the companions of the left.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِـَٔايَٰتِنَا", "translit": "āَnِtَٰyāَٔـِb", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "أَصْحَٰبُ", "translit": "ُbَٰḥْṣَaʾ", "root": "صحب"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ٱلْمَشْـَٔمَةِ", "translit": "ِẗَmَٔـْhsَmْlٱ", "root": "شام"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "عَلَيْهِمْ نَارٌ مُّؤْصَدَةٌۢ ", "translation": "Over them will be fire closed in.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "نَارٌ", "translit": "ٌrāَn", "root": "نور"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُّؤْصَدَةٌۢ", "translit": "ٌۢẗَdَṣْwʾُّm", "root": "وصد"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"8": [{"arabic": "ولذلك امتن عليه فقال ألم نجعل له عينين ولسانا وشفتين وهديناه النجدين وعرف خسته أولا فقال {ألم يك نطفة من مني يمنى ثم كان علقة} ثم ذكر منته عليه فقال {فخلق فسوى فجعل منه الزوجين الذكر والأنثى} ليدوم وجوده بالتناسل كما حصل وجوده أولا بالاختراع فمن كان هذا بدؤه وهذه أحواله فمن أين له البطر والكبرياء والفخر والخيلاء وهو على التحقيق أخس الأخساء وأضعف الضعفاء ولكن هذه عادة الخسيس إذا رفع من خسته شمخ بأنفه وتعظم وذلك لدلالة خسة أوله ولا حول ولا قوة إلا بالله نعم لو أكمله وفوض إليه أمره وأدام له الوجود باختياره لجاز أن يطغى وينس", "english": "As for his end and his final destination — it is death, indicated by the saying of God Most High: {ثم أماته فأقبره ثم إذا شاء أنشره} — \"Then He caused him to die and buried him; then, when He wills, He shall raise him.\" Its meaning is that He strips from him his spirit, his hearing, his sight, his knowledge, his power, his sense, his perception, and his movement — so he returns to being an inert thing (jamād), just as he was the first time, with nothing remaining except the shape of his limbs and his form — no sense in him, no movement. Then he is placed in the earth, and becomes a putrid, filthy carcass, just as he was at first a contemptible drop. Then his limbs decay, his parts crumble, his bones rot, and he becomes dust and fragments; the worm eats his parts — beginning with his two pupils, plucking them out; then his cheeks, cutting them away; then the rest of his parts — until he becomes dung in the bellies of worms, a carcass from which the animal flees, which every man deems filthy and shuns for the intensity of its stench. And the best of his states is that he returns to what he was: he becomes earth, from which jugs are made and from which buildings are made. So he becomes nonexistent after having been existent, and becomes as though he had never flourished yesterday — reaped down — just as he was in his first affair for a long span. And would that he had remained so — how good it would be if he were left as earth!", "book_title": "Condemnation of Pride and Conceit", "section_title_ar": "Section 864", "section_title_en": "On the Baseness of Man's Origin and the Folly of Pride — Section 864 of The Revival of the Religious Sciences", "section_index": 864, "anchors": "- Root: ض ل ل (ḍ-l-l)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core sense of going astray, being lost, or perishing; also used for being concealed or obliterated.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): In theological context, denotes deviation from the straight path (al-ṣirāṭ al-mustaqīm) and the state of being bereft of divine guidance — here, the primordial state of non-existence is framed as utter loss.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) for physical straying; metaphorical (majāz) for spiritual ruin — applied here to the pre-creation void.\n- Root: ن ط ف (n-ṭ-f)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Water that flows or drips; a drop; specifically the seminal fluid.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"النطفة: الماء الصافي، ويعبر بها عن ماء الرجل\" — pure water, used as a euphemism for male semen; also the pearl (al-luʾluʾah) in its purity, but here contrasted with filth (qadhir).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for clear water; metaphorical for the base origin of man — the drop is both physically and morally negligible.\n- Root: م ل ك (m-l-k)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Possession, dominion, and control; the hand that grasps and holds.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Ownership and sovereign power; in Kalam, distinguishes the Creator's absolute dominion (mulk) from the creature's borrowed, contingent capacity.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for legal possession; metaphorical for self-mastery — man \"does not possess his own heart\" (lā yamliku qalbahu), a rhetorical denial of autonomous agency.\n- Root: ك ب ر (k-b-r)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Greatness in size, rank, or dignity; also arrogance (kibr) as its blameworthy derivative.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Grandeur (kibriyāʾ) is exclusively divine; human pride is a usurpation of an attribute that belongs to God alone.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal for physical magnitude; metaphorical for moral haughtiness — the text pivots on this tension.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The repeated use of \"إنما\" (only, solely) in the opening lines restricts the cause of man's creation and blessing to a single purpose: self-knowledge and knowledge of God, not self-glorification.", "content_type": "ethics", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on purifying the character, moral diseases, and spiritual remedies, from 'Condemnation of Pride and Conceit'", "badge": "Ethics"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 540, 2678], [2, 2678, 3820], [3, 3820, 5328], [4, 5328, 6350]], "90:1": [[1, 540, 2678], [2, 2678, 3820], [3, 3820, 5328], [4, 5328, 6350]], "2": [[1, 200, 1928], [2, 1928, 2807], [3, 2807, 4788], [4, 4788, 6130]], "90:2": [[1, 200, 1928], [2, 1928, 2807], [3, 2807, 4788], [4, 4788, 6130]], "3": [[1, 250, 2174], [2, 2174, 3409], [3, 3409, 